# What never enters a build context.
#
# Both Dockerfiles build from the REPOSITORY ROOT, because each needs files from more than one
# directory — build/docker/ragcore.Dockerfile copies ragcore/pyproject.toml, ragcore/uv.lock and
# ragcore/src/, and the .NET one copies dotnet/. A root context means everything below is sent to
# the daemon unless it is excluded here.
#
# THIS FILE IS A SECURITY CONTROL, NOT A BUILD OPTIMISATION, and the difference matters. The
# optimisation is real — ragcore/.venv and node_modules are hundreds of megabytes that would be
# uploaded on every build — but the reason each entry is here is that a file in the context can end
# up in an image layer, and a file in a layer is readable by anyone who can pull it. A local
# .env, a developer's Azure token cache or the .git directory in an image is a credential leak that
# no scanner of the running container would notice, because the process never reads the file.
#
# Deny nothing broadly and allow back: an allow-list here would silently drop a file the build
# genuinely needs, and the failure would be a missing module at runtime.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version control and CI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .git carries every secret ever committed and then removed. It is the single most valuable thing
# in this list.
.git/
.github/
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local environments and dependency trees
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The virtual environment is rebuilt inside the builder from uv.lock. Copying a developer's one in
# would also copy whatever platform-specific wheels it happens to hold.
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/dist/
**/build/lib/
**/*.egg-info/
apps/web/dist/
apps/desktop/out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything that could hold a credential
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No deployed configuration comes from a file: every secret is a Key Vault reference resolved
# through managed identity at the point of use. A .env in a context is therefore always a
# developer's local file, and never something an image should carry.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.pfx
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/.azure/
**/.aws/
**/.kube/
**/secrets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and operating system noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Things that are documentation rather than product
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Excluded so a documentation edit does not invalidate the build cache, and so an image carries no
# internal design material. The specification describes controls in detail, which is useful to a
# reviewer and equally useful to somebody probing the running system.
docs/
specs/
*.md
!README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The production image installs with --no-dev and runs no tests. Excluding them keeps the test
# fixtures — which contain deliberately realistic-looking fake credentials — out of every layer.
ragcore/tests/
dotnet/tests/
apps/web/**/*.spec.ts
